Next, the script adds three types of constraints: each city is visited exactly once, each city is left exactly once, and the subtour elimination constraints. The subtour elimination constraints use the Miller-Tucker-Zemlin (MTZ) method to ensure that the solution does not contain any subtours.

Finally, the script solves the model and outputs the minimum total travel cost and the optimal route (if an optimal solution is found).

