### Decision Variables:
- \(x_{ij}\): The quantity of product \(j\) processed on equipment \(i\), where \(i\) represents the equipment (A1, A2, B1, B2, B3) and \(j\) represents the product (I, II, III).

### Objective Function:
- Maximize profit: \[Z = \sum_{i \in \{A1, A2, B1, B2, B3\}}\sum_{j \in \{I, II, III\}} (unit price_j - unit processing time_{ij} \times unit cost) \times x_{ij} - \sum_{i \in \{A1, A2, B1, B2, B3\}} equipment cost_i \times \frac{\sum_{j \in \{I, II, III\}} x_{ij}}{equipment available time_i}\]
  - This function calculates the total profit based on the quantity of each product processed on each equipment, the unit price, unit processing time, and unit cost, as well as the equipment cost and available time.

### Constraints:
1. Equipment processing time constraints:
   - \(\sum_{j \in \{I, II, III\}} x_{ij} \leq equipment available time_i, \forall i\)
2. Non-negativity constraints:
   - \(x_{ij} \geq 0, \forall i, j\)

### Integer Constraints:
- \(x_{ij}\) must be integers, as the quantity of products cannot be fractional.

