model.addConstr(cp.quicksum(x[i] for i in courses if courses[i]['computer'] == 1) >= 2, name="ComputerCourses")

# Prerequisites
model.addConstr(x['Business Statistics'] <= x['Calculus'], name="BusinessStatisticsPrerequisite")
model.addConstr(x['Computer Simulation'] <= x['Introduction to Computer Programming'], name="ComputerSimulationPrerequisite")
model.addConstr(x['Data Structures'] <= x['Introduction to Computer Programming'], name="DataStructuresPrerequisite")
model.addConstr(x['Forecasting'] <= x['Business Statistics'], name="ForecastingPrerequisite")

# Solve the model
model.solve()

# Output the results
if model.status == COPT.OPTIMAL:
    print("Minimum number of courses: {}".format(model.objval))
    print("Selected courses:")
    for i in courses:
        if x[i].x == 1:
            print(f"  {i}")
else:
    print("No optimal solution found.")
```

This script first defines the courses and their requirements, then creates a binary decision variable for each course, indicating whether the course is taken. The objective function is to minimize the number of courses, and the constraints ensure that at least two math courses, two OR courses, and two computer courses are taken, as well as satisfying the prerequisites.

Finally, the script solves the model and outputs the minimum number of courses and the selected courses. This provides students with an optimized course selection strategy to satisfy the major requirements with the least number of courses.
