### Decision Variables:
- \(y_i\): Whether to open the warehouse in city \(i\). If the warehouse is opened, \(y_i = 1\); otherwise, \(y_i = 0\). Here, \(i\) can be any of New York, Los Angeles, Chicago, or Atlanta.
- \(x_{ij}\): The number of units shipped from city \(i\) to region \(j\). Here, \(i\) can be any of New York, Los Angeles, Chicago, or Atlanta, and \(j\) can be any of region 1, region 2, or region 3.

### Objective Function:
- Minimize total cost: \[Z = 400y_{\text{New York}} + 500y_{\text{Los Angeles}} + 300y_{\text{Chicago}} + 150y_{\text{Atlanta}} + \sum_{i \in \{\text{New York, Los Angeles, Chicago, Atlanta}\}}\sum_{j=1}^{3} (cost_{ij} \times x_{ij})\]
  - This function calculates the total cost of opening warehouses and shipping units from each city to each region.

