The objective function is to minimize the total costs, which is the sum of the costs of regular-time production, overtime production, and inventory for each month.

The constraints include demand satisfaction, ensuring that the demand for each month is met by the sum of regular-time production, overtime production, and inventory from the previous month, and production capacity constraints, ensuring that the production quantities do not exceed the production capacity of regular-time and overtime.

Finally, the script solves the model and outputs the optimal solution (if found). It prints the minimum total cost and the optimal production and inventory quantities for each month.

