   - This ensures that the demand of each region is met.
2. Warehouse capacity: \[x_{ij} \leq 100y_i, \forall i, j\]
   - This ensures that the number of units shipped from each warehouse does not exceed its capacity.
3. Warehouse opening constraints:
   - If the New York warehouse is opened, then the Los Angeles warehouse must be opened: \(y_{\text{New York}} \leq y_{\text{Los Angeles}}\)
   - At most two warehouses can be opened: \(\sum_{i \in \{\text{New York, Los Angeles, Chicago, Atlanta}\}} y_i \leq 2\)
   - Either the Atlanta or the Los Angeles warehouse must be opened: \(y_{\text{Atlanta}} + y_{\text{Los Angeles}} \geq 1\)

