The objective function is to minimize the total cost, which is the sum of the product of the proportion of each fertilizer and its price.

The constraints include the lower bounds on the nitrogen, phosphorus, and potash content, as well as the upper bounds on these chemical contents. Additionally, there is a constraint to ensure that the total proportion of all fertilizers in the mix is 1.

Finally, the script solves the model and outputs the minimum total cost and the optimal fertilizer mix proportions.

